  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$x^2+3 x+2=\\min \\{|x-3|,|x+2|\\}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4NjyNczt6hiZcFfSaMKKfslWVTOk3-7bH87VHxFl65o.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& y=x^2+3 x+2 \\\\\n& y=x^2+2\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right) x+\\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{9}{4}+2 \\\\\n& y=\\left(x+\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n& y+\\frac{1}{4}=\\left(x+\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\text { Parabola vertex }\\left(\\frac{-3}{2}, \\frac{-1}{4}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\Rightarrow$ By graph 2 solution possible",
    "image": null
  },
